quotes.quote:
**Safe rename — proposed ProtoJSON PATCH body:**

```json
{
  "campaign": {
    "name": "campaigns/C7",
    "displayName": "Summer"
  },
  "updateMask": "displayName"
}
```

Expected stored resource:

```json
{
  "name": "campaigns/C7",
  "displayName": "Summer",
  "description": "Approved",
  "spendLimitMicros": "25000000"
}

**Intentional description reset — independently starting from the original before state:**

```json
{
  "campaign": {
    "name": "campaigns/C7",
    "description": ""
  },
  "updateMask": "description"
}
```

Expected stored resource:

```json
{
  "name": "campaigns/C7",
  "displayName": "Spring",
  "description": "",
  "spendLimitMicros": "25000000"
}
```

These masks are resource-relative ProtoJSON strings. `name` identifies the resource; it is not selected for mutation. Under this specific contract, resetting also works if serialization omits the empty description: the selected, absent scalar still becomes `""`. Omission without the mask has different consequences.
